    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Interpretation Guide\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### What Do the Attention Weights Mean?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **High Attention (Red/Yellow in Jet colormap)**: Regions that the attentive probe prioritizes when making predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Low Attention (Blue/Purple)**: Regions that are less important for the classification task\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Key Observations to Look For\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Anatomical Specificity**: Does attention focus on clinically relevant structures (e.g., cardiac chambers)?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Temporal Consistency**: Is attention stable across frames or does it shift?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Spatial Coherence**: Are high-attention regions localized or scattered?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Background Suppression**: Is the model suppressing background/non-cardiac regions?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Debugging Tips\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"If attention appears uniform:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Check that the hook is properly extracting weights (add debug prints)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Verify the spatial grid dimensions (H_patch, W_patch) are correct\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Ensure the classifier is properly loaded and in eval mode\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"If attention is too concentrated:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- This might indicate overfitting or a very specific feature\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Try adjusting the `HEATMAP_ALPHA` parameter to see the frame better\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Next Steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Quantify Attention**: Compute entropy or concentration metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Compare Classes**: Visualize attention for different disease classes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Ablation Study**: Mask high-attention regions and measure prediction change\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Multi-Head Analysis**: Compare attention across different classifier heads\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
